From 61f93d4e9523b143595eab9560cd9f306791fb3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Alef <476570+calef@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:31:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rsext4)!: decode group descriptors instead of casting

BlockGroupDescTable::get_desc and BlockGroupDescTableMut::get_desc_mut
cast a byte offset in the table to &Ext4GroupDesc. That reference is
undefined behavior when the table bytes are not 4-byte aligned, reads
the fields in native byte order, and always spans 64 bytes. With
32-byte descriptors it reads the next record as the high halves, it
returns None for the last record of an exactly sized table, and every
update through the mutable view writes high halves into the next
record.

Both views now decode the record's own desc_size bytes with
Ext4GroupDesc::decode_checked and the mutable view writes them back
with encode_checked, so the 32-byte and 64-byte (and larger)
descriptor sizes each touch only their own record.

BREAKING CHANGE: get_desc returns Option<Ext4GroupDesc> by value,
BlockGroupDescIter yields Ext4GroupDesc, and get_desc_mut is replaced
by get_desc and set_desc on BlockGroupDescTableMut.
---
 fs/rsext4/src/blockgroup_description/table.rs | 126 +++++++++---------
 fs/rsext4/src/blockgroup_description/tests.rs | 114 ++++++++++++++++
 fs/rsext4/src/test_contracts.rs               |   2 +-
 3 files changed, 179 insertions(+), 63 deletions(-)

